## Why This Is Asked
Tests basic Android data persistence and UI wiring using familiar components.

## Key Concepts
- Room: Entity, DAO, database
- LiveData and ViewModel
- Repository pattern
- Prepopulation via RoomDatabase.Callback
- Rotation handling with LiveData

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity
data class Task(
  @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,
  val text: String,
  val done: Boolean = false
)
@Dao
interface TaskDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM Task") fun getAll(): LiveData<List<Task>>
  @Insert fun insert(task: Task): Long
  @Delete fun delete(task: Task)
}
@Database(entities = [Task::class], version = 1)
abstract class AppDb : RoomDatabase() {
  abstract fun taskDao(): TaskDao
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test prepopulation and DAO methods?
- How would you migration plan for Task schema changes?

## Why This Is Asked

New angle introduces multi-cache offline view and scheduled refresh, probing data modeling, cache invalidation, and basic MVVM patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Room entities and relations
- Separate body cache design
- MVVM with Repository
- WorkManager with constraints
- Simple search SQL LIKE

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "article_meta")
data class ArticleMeta(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val excerpt: String,
  val updatedAt: Long
)

@Entity(tableName = "article_body")
data class ArticleBody(
  @PrimaryKey val articleId: String,
  val body: String
)

@Dao
interface ArticleDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM article_meta WHERE title LIKE :query || '%'")
  fun searchByTitle(query: String): List<ArticleMeta>

  @Transaction
  @Query("SELECT * FROM article_meta WHERE id = :id")
  fun getArticleWithBody(id: String): ArticleWithBody
}
```

