## Why This Is Asked
Tests offline-first design, conflict resolution, and Android architecture (Room, WorkManager), plus privacy controls.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first data model with Room encryption
- Vector clocks for per-conversation conflict resolution
- WorkManager pipelines with network constraints and retries

## Code Example
```kotlin
data class VectorClock(val map: MutableMap<String, Long>) {
  fun merge(other: VectorClock): VectorClock {
    val result = map.toMutableMap()
    for ((k, v) in other.map) {
      result[k] = maxOf(result.getOrDefault(k, 0L), v)
    }
    return VectorClock(result)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle multi-device clocks and out-of-order messages?
- What tests would validate partitioning and eventual consistency?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes real-world offline-first sync patterns, deterministic conflict resolution, and Android tooling (Room, WorkManager). It tests handling intermittent connectivity, battery constraints, and data consistency.

## Key Concepts
- Room model with lastModified, serverVersion, and dirty flags
- WorkManager with constraints and exponential backoff
- Conflict resolution: last-writer-wins with a deterministic tie-breaker
- End-to-end testing: MockWebServer, offline simulation, and backoff verification

## Code Example
```javascript
function resolveNoteConflict(local, remote) {
  if (local.lastModified > remote.lastModified) return local;
  if (remote.lastModified > local.lastModified) return remote;
  // equal timestamps -> use serverVersion as tie-breaker
  return remote.serverVersion >= local.serverVersion ? remote : local;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle partial failures of pushes or streaming updates?
- How would you adapt the model for collaborative edits from multiple devices?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests cross-process IPC, privacy-preserving on-device ML, and production-minded governance. It requires a concrete IPC surface, encrypted storage, opt-in controls, and a comprehensive plan for updates and testing.

## Key Concepts
- Android isolated process and AIDL IPC for secure communication
- Encryption at rest using Android Keystore with AES-256
- Encrypted Room storage for inputs and model state
- On-device ML with TensorFlow Lite
- Update orchestration under Doze, Wi-Fi/charging constraints with rollback support

## Code Example
```javascript
